From dc6abb1d0c63252b846ef1e65942314842f768ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tessera CI <ci@tessera.test>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:30:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ml): point-in-time card_chargeback_rate and the four
 validation gates

fraud-v3 reached shadow with card_chargeback_rate built as a whole-table
groupby over chargeback_filed_at, a column that is non-null only on fraud
rows and arrives 20-89 days late. Offline that scored AUC 0.906; served
point-in-time in shadow it scored 0.699 against a champion's 0.778
(TESS-2310).

ml/features/aggregates.py -- card_chargeback_rate(df, as_of) counts only
chargebacks filed strictly before the as-of instant, over that card's
transactions that had happened strictly before it. Takes a scalar cutoff
(how the nightly card_history batch serves it) or one instant per row (how a
training table is built). Both bounds strict, so a row cannot count its own
chargeback and tied timestamps cannot change the answer. Reproduces the
investigation's shares exactly: non-zero on 3.44% of training rows and
14.19% of scored rows.

ml/validation/ -- the four gates model-validation.yml already specified,
with exactly its flags. Gate 1 checks every feature by taking the future
away: permute the label, censor chargebacks not yet filed at the cutoff,
delete rows from after the cutoff, and fail if any value moves.
ml/validation/tests/negative_fixtures.py keeps notebook 01's definition so
the gate is tested by watching it fail on it.

ml/fraud/MODEL_CARD.md -- the numbers MRM should see. Point-in-time the
candidate scores PR-AUC 0.1590 against the champion's 0.1640, and the
feature itself is worth -0.0012 PR-AUC. Recommendation: keep the promotion
blocked, drop the feature, give device_card_count an as-of cut and re-run.

All four gates pass on the synthetic table; uv run pytest ml/ is 57 green.

